{%- set first = variants.0 -%}
# {{ theme.name }} Starship Theme

Starship prompt themes for {{ theme.name }}. {{ theme.description }}

## Installation

Add the palette to your Starship config:

```bash
cat {{ theme.id }}-{{ first.variant.id }}.toml >> ~/.config/starship.toml
```

Then set the palette in your config:

```toml
palette = '{{ theme.id }}-{{ first.variant.id }}'
```
{% for v in variants | slice(start=1) %}
Or for {{ v.variant.id }}:

```bash
cat {{ theme.id }}-{{ v.variant.id }}.toml >> ~/.config/starship.toml
```

```toml
palette = '{{ theme.id }}-{{ v.variant.id }}'
```
{% endfor %}
## How It Works

This overrides Starship's standard named colors, so your existing module configurations will automatically use {{ theme.name }} colors without any changes.

